WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Welcome to the SmartLingo first-time tour. In about ten minutes, you will see the experience designed for a new visitor and the full workflow available after sign-in. The first half requires no account. The second half uses a dedicated test member. No real email address, password, or verification code appears anywhere in this recording.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Part one begins as a signed-out visitor. The home page offers four clear destinations: Learn, Practice, Speak, and Community. You can try Everyday speaking, Learn through play, browse courses, or ask the AI Guru before creating an account. Anonymous practice stays outside the member database, so you can explore first and decide when you are ready.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:13.011
On the Learn page, choose the language and learning path that fit your goal. SmartLingo connects vocabulary, reading, writing, listening, and speaking instead of isolating them. Beginner content starts with easier and more frequent words, then considers school grade and difficulty. New sentences reuse words from the current and previous rounds, so the experience does not suddenly jump beyond your vocabulary.

00:01:13.011 --> 00:01:37.358
Learn through play brings together Today's Sprint, SmartCard practice, SmartCard Challenge, rankings, course-credit redemption, and the free Beginner trial. A signed-out visitor chooses a language again inside each activity. This prevents the language selected in one product from silently carrying into another. Except for the timed challenge, each learning item shows feedback before you choose Continue.

00:01:37.358 --> 00:02:01.358
Open Today's Sprint, then choose the target language, today's practice time, and a starting day. Ten minutes is the default, with one five-skill round for every five minutes. The day control covers a planned twenty-one-day progression and lets you move backward or forward. Starting a new anonymous Sprint clears temporary status, while extending the timer keeps the current round.

00:02:01.358 --> 00:02:26.572
Today's Sprint mixes picture vocabulary, listening, reading, writing, sentence building, and speaking. Selecting an answer immediately opens the correct or incorrect review; there is no extra Check step. Sentence-building exercises provide at least two more choices than the completed sentence needs and evaluate automatically when every space is filled. Prompts prefer words already learned in this round or earlier rounds.

00:02:26.572 --> 00:02:51.904
SmartCard practice organizes a high-frequency bank into twenty-one learning days. Beginner words use pictures whenever a concrete idea can be represented accurately; a clear generic visual supports abstract function words. Every card shows difficulty, frequency, and school-grade information. Ordering begins with easier vocabulary, then uses frequency and grade to surface the most useful words first.

00:02:51.904 --> 00:03:15.904
SmartCard Challenge is a timed game, so it does not stop for a Continue button. Choose Beginner, Intermediate, or Advanced. The system creates the fixed daily set for your local calendar date, which means each region has its own local midnight boundary. An answer shows a short result and automatically advances. Sign in to save the score and enter the correct language-and-level ranking.

00:03:15.904 --> 00:03:43.437
Everyday speaking starts with real places such as an airport, hotel, restaurant, cafe, grocery store, hospital, bank, and school. Each place offers Beginner, Intermediate, and Advanced material. Lessons use connected question-and-answer conversations, not isolated phrases. Repeat after me is off by default, so the page does not request microphone access until you intentionally enable speaking and scoring.

00:03:43.437 --> 00:04:07.559
Community remains useful before sign-in. Visitors can understand language discussions, Nearby learning, and rankings without hitting a blank page or forced login. Nearby is adult opt-in and uses only a broad city or region, never precise GPS coordinates. When no real learner is available, clearly labeled AI classmates are ready to practice without pretending to be human.

00:04:07.559 --> 00:04:35.130
The course catalog lists administrator-managed language programs at three levels. Beginner develops core vocabulary, pronunciation, listening, and guided speech. Intermediate expands real-life conversation and writing. Advanced adds accent work, presentations, and expression coaching. The platform sets course pricing consistently and the first month is free. Browsing is public; secure account access begins only when you subscribe.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:59.276
All courses are built into SmartLingo and maintained by the platform administrator. Choose a learning language, then select Beginner, Intermediate, or Advanced access for three, six, or twelve months. Members do not create separate course catalogs, so learning content, prices, progress, and certificates remain consistent.

00:04:59.276 --> 00:05:23.276
When you are ready to save progress, select Sign in or join. Password is the default method; you can switch to an email verification code on the same page. If a requested code does not arrive in the inbox, check Spam or Junk. The code applies only to that sign-in attempt, and this tour never enters or reveals a real code.

00:05:23.276 --> 00:05:47.454
If email codes are inconvenient, choose Use password instead. Enter an email and a password of at least eight characters. A new address creates an ordinary member account immediately, while an existing password account signs in. The eye control lets you inspect what you typed. Forgot password sends a one-time reset code; SmartLingo never emails or silently assigns a temporary password.

00:05:47.454 --> 00:06:11.454
Part two switches to a dedicated test member. After sign-in, learning progress, course access, twenty-one-day memory, scores, and certificate records can be saved securely to the member account. Email-code and password access continue to coexist and lead to the same Dashboard. The test identity is masked in this video while the real member interface remains visible.

00:06:11.454 --> 00:06:35.454
The Dashboard is the signed-in learning home. Today's Sprint appears first. SmartCard practice, SmartCard Challenge, Everyday speaking, and subscribed Courses follow as separate sections. Each product can add its own target language, so choosing Japanese for one tool does not force Japanese onto every other tool. The Courses section uses Add course to open the language and level catalog.

00:06:35.454 --> 00:06:59.454
When a member opens Today's Sprint, the app reads the last saved day, round, and skill status from the database. You can continue directly or use the first, previous, next, and last-day controls to choose another starting point. After each item, the review explains the result and waits for Continue, so useful feedback never disappears before you can read it.

00:06:59.454 --> 00:07:24.718
View score history organizes daily results by Today's Sprint, SmartCard Challenge, course level, and other learning categories. Each record separates the language, date, learning score, and reward source. This makes it easier to see which skills improve consistently and which need another review. Learning XP represents motivation and progress; it is not cash and it is not an official examination score.

00:07:24.718 --> 00:07:50.501
The learning calendar places completed practice, planned work, and needs-review items on one timeline. Missed words and sentences return in later review rather than disappearing permanently. Reading, listening, and writing continue to reuse mastered or currently learning vocabulary, then expand gradually. This keeps the learner in a productive difficulty range instead of interrupting the session with an unexpectedly advanced sentence.

00:07:50.501 --> 00:08:14.501
My courses shows only the programs joined or subscribed by the current member. Each course separates vocabulary, reading, writing, listening, and speaking while sharing the same vocabulary ordering, review feedback, and Continue behavior. To add another language or level, choose Course to return to the public catalog. Existing progress remains intact when a new course is added.

00:08:14.501 --> 00:08:40.648
Members can find real learners who explicitly opt in, or begin immediately with an AI classmate. AI participants are always labeled and never impersonate people. Community provides discussions, shared missions, and rankings. Real-member cards include block and report controls. Social activity supports practice, but it can never alter verified course scores or payment records.

00:08:40.648 --> 00:09:05.561
The Message Center supports private conversations, group chat, and course communication. You can enter a conversation from Community or a course, then use replies, attachments, notifications, and safety reports. Guru can polish a draft before you send it. Live voice and microphone access begin only after you intentionally open a compatible speaking activity and accept the device permission.

00:09:05.561 --> 00:09:30.272
Account settings include display name, interface language, site-wide text size, and the preferred text AI provider. A code-only account sees Add password and no current-password field. A password-enabled account sees Update password and must enter the current password. Adding or updating a password does not require another email code, and every password field includes an accessible show-or-hide control.

00:09:30.272 --> 00:09:57.143
If you forget the password, choose Forgot password in password mode, enter the account email, receive a one-time reset code, and select a new password of at least eight characters. The platform never creates, stores, or emails a temporary password. After recovery, email-code sign-in remains available. Password access and verification-code access are two continuing choices, not mutually exclusive account types.

00:09:57.143 --> 00:10:21.392
That is the SmartLingo first-time workflow. Begin anonymously with Today's Sprint, SmartCards, or Everyday speaking. When you want to save a score, join with an email code or a password. After sign-in, resume from the Dashboard, review history, join Community, and manage courses from one place. Choose a language you genuinely want to use, and speak your first sentence today.
